source.exactNormativeText:
[p125]     4.24.    BUILD-024 Builder Output
[p125] 
[p125] 
[p125] The final output of the Pricing Builder is structured pricing work that can be consumed
[p125] consistently by subsequent MVP capabilities.
[p125] 
[p125] Where applicable, the Builder output must preserve:
[p125] 
[p125]    ● pricing action;
[p125]    ● affected pricing scope;
[p125]    ● relevant pricing baseline;
[p125]    ● structured pricing logic;
[p125]    ● calculation inputs;
[p125]    ● explicit assumptions;
[p125]    ● material parameters;
[p125]    ● conditions;
[p125]    ● constraints;
[p125]    ● references to applicable organisational Guardrails and, where available, their
[p125]        authoritative ANALYSIS-014 evaluation results;
[p125]    ● exceptions;
[p125]    ● deterministic calculation status;
[p125]    ● applicable calculation method;
[p125]    ● resulting proposed pricing output;
[p125]    ● distinction between system-calculated values and manually determined or qualitative
[p125]        components.
[p125] 
[p126] Organisational Guardrail references contained in Builder output must point to the applicable
[p126] governance-defined Guardrail rather than represent a separately authored Builder Guardrail.
[p126] 
[p126] Where an ANALYSIS-014 evaluation is not yet available, the Builder output may preserve
[p126] the applicable Guardrail reference without inventing an evaluation result.
[p126] 
[p126] For deterministically calculable pricing work, the Builder output must contain sufficient
[p126] information for the analytical layer to reproduce the result using the calculation definitions in
[p126] Section 3.5.
[p126] 
[p126] For pricing work that contains non-deterministic components, the output must preserve those
[p126] components without falsely converting them into calculated quantitative results.
[p126] 
[p126] The Builder output must provide sufficient information for:
[p126] 
[p126]    ● pricing analysis;
[p126]    ● Scenario evaluation;
[p126]    ● collaboration;
[p126]    ● review;
[p126]    ● Pricing Proposal creation;
[p126]    ● organisational decision;
[p126]    ● execution preparation;
[p126]    ● historical understanding.
[p126] 
[p126] The Pricing Builder therefore serves as the controlled bridge between a business pricing
[p126] objective and the specific pricing action ultimately submitted for organisational decision.
[p126]

